# A Snake game, written down move by move.
#
# Lines that are not comments are commands, exactly as they are typed at the
# prompt. Undo and redo are moves like any other, so reading this file back
# retraces the game as it was really played - second thoughts and all - and
# arrives at the same position it was saved from.
#
# The deal line says how many were playing, what they were dealt from, and who
# was in each seat - 'you' for a person here, a skill for the program.
#
#   dotnet run -- snake replay <this file>

deal 1 8913973772283777877 you

#   1  turn 1, Snake A
go

#   2  turn 2, Snake A
go

#   3  turn 3, Snake A
go

#   4  turn 4, Snake A
a west
#      A snake cannot turn back into its own neck, and west is the way this one came. The other three are open.

#   5  turn 4, Snake A
go

#   6  turn 5, Snake A
go

#   7  turn 6, Snake A
go

#   8  turn 7, Snake A
go

#   9  turn 8, Snake A
a west
#      A snake cannot turn back into its own neck, and west is the way this one came. The other three are open.

#  10  turn 8, Snake A
go

#  11  turn 9, Snake A
go

#  12  turn 10, Snake A
go

#  13  turn 11, Snake A
go

#  14  turn 12, Snake A
a north
#      Snake A turns north.

#  15  turn 12, Snake A
a west
#      Snake A turns west.

#  16  turn 12, Snake A
go
#      Snake A ran into itself.
#      The game is over: nothing is left moving.

